Question 4:
a)fork() It creates a new child process by duplicating the existing calling process (the parent). The child process gets a separate memory space but inherits copies of the parent's data,
stack, heap, and open file descriptors.
exec() It replaces the current process memory image with a brand-new program. When a process calls exec(), its current code, data are completely overwritten by the
new executable program. No new process is created;the process ID (PID) remains the exact same.
